  "description": "<p>GSearch: solve the truncated special characters problem. Proposed by Leire Urcelay:</p>\n\n<p>\"<br/>\nWhen doing a search, the fields having field.lenght &gt; fieldMaxLength are truncated using getBestFragments method. </p>\n\n<p>If the field contains some special characters, like &apos;, it can happen that this special character is cut.</p>\n\n<p>For example, the field â€œIl est donc intÃ©ressant de se pencher sur l'acquisitionâ€ is transformed into â€œIl est donc intÃ©ressant de se pencher sur l &amp;apos ... â€œ.</p>\n\n<p>This transformation should produce an error during the XSLT transformation. Currently, this is not the case, since there is a strange transformation in the code. In fact, all â€œ&amp;â€ characters are transformed in â€œ#â€ character.</p>\n\n<p>You can see it in the method executeQuery of the class Statement.java:</p>\n\n<p>     snippets = highlighter.getBestFragments(tokenStream, f.stringValue(), snippetsMax, \" ... \");</p>\n\n<p>     snippets = snippets.replace('&amp;', '#');</p>\n\n<p>Due to this character replacement, there is not any error in the xsl transformation, but however, there is a problem when displaying the result. Instead of getting:</p>\n\n<p>â€œIl est donc intÃ©ressant de se pencher sur lâ€™ ...â€</p>\n\n<p>The following is displayed:</p>\n\n<p>â€œIl est donc intÃ©ressant de se pencher sur l #apos ...â€<br/>\n\"</p>\n\n<p>The current solution with '#' was a tradeoff. A more satisfactory solution should be included in the next version of GSearch.</p>",
